    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nChanged the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence:\n\n- **`OwnerCustomerCodes`** \u2014 `format` now takes `city, lastName, sequence` and emits `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`. The three-letter prefix logic was already parameterized, so I generalized the private `prefix` helper (from `lastName` to a generic `value`) and reused it for both city and last name rather than duplicating it.\n\n- **`AssignOwnerCustomerCode`** \u2014 the 4-digit sequence is now *per city*: one more than the number of existing owners already in the same city (counted from `findAll()`), instead of a global count. Passes the city through to the formatter.\n\n- **`OwnerMapper.membershipNumber`** \u2014 no logic change needed: it already builds off `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so the membership number (and any other value derived from the code) automatically rebuilds on the new format. I only updated the Javadoc example to `LON-SMI-0007-M26`.\n\nThe new acceptance test (`coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix`, asserting `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) and the full suite pass.",
